## What changed

Adds a complete preliminary research project for NG-StateMin-U1 under `projects/ng-statemin-u1/`.

- reusable PyTorch implementation of `s_t = min(x_t - s_{t-1}, -x_t)`;
- algebraic and gradient tests;
- compact comparison benchmark against scalar ReLU/tanh recurrences, Elman RNNs, and GRU;
- experimental report and reported results table;
- project README, MIT license, citation metadata, and AI-use disclosure;
- dedicated GitHub Actions workflow for Python 3.10 and 3.12;
- portfolio index update.

## Why

The candidate law exhibits an exact period-two memory regime with temporal state derivatives restricted to `-1` or `0`. The project also documents the central negative result: severe odd/even sequence-length dependence. Claims are deliberately presented as preliminary rather than state of the art.

## Validation

GitHub Actions passed on Python 3.10 and 3.12:

- package installation;
- Ruff lint;
- five Pytest tests;
- smoke benchmark for NG-StateMin-U1 and U1-ReLU.

## Scientific caution

This pull request does not claim established literature-level novelty or a general replacement for RNN, GRU, or LSTM cells. It publishes a reproducible artifact and a defensible starting point for a phase-corrected U2 follow-up.
